# Astro: confirm this boot to the bootloader (docs/05 §4, AD-011).
# Runs `rauc status mark-good` (with retries) once the boot-success
# milestone is reached, resetting the attempt counters
# (BOOT_x_LEFT / x_TRY). If boot-success is never reached, this never
# runs, the counters keep decrementing across reboots, and the
# bootloader falls back to the other slot after 3 attempts.

# before login.target (M3 phase 2, with boot-success's same clause):
# dinit's console log stops at login.target (runs-on-console), and the
# OK line of whatever starts LAST before the handover can race the
# acquisition and vanish from serial. With mark-good ordered before
# login, the boot-success line has flushed by the time the console is
# released (mark-good spans real D-Bus work), and the login prompt only
# appears once this boot is confirmed good — which is also the honest
# ordering. On a bad slot boot-success fails, this never runs, and
# login proceeds after the failure resolves (AD-011 watchdog rules).
before: login.target

type = scripted
command = /usr/libexec/astro/mark-good
depends-on: boot-success
depends-on: bootenv-mount
waits-for: rauc
